  <Placemark>
   <name>Special Marine Warning issued September 15 at 8:16PM EDT until September 15 at 8:30PM EDT by NWS Key West FL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>For the following areas...
Gulf Waters from East Cape Sable to Chokoloskee 20 to 60 nm out and
beyond 5 fathoms...

At 815 PM EDT, a strong thunderstorm was located 8 nm west of P
Tower, moving southwest at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts 34 knots or greater.

SOURCE...National Weather Service Meteorologist.

IMPACT...Expect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots, suddenly higher
waves, frequent lightning, and heavy downpours.

The strong thunderstorm will remain over mainly open waters.</Snippet>
