   <name>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 15 at 8:16PM EDT until September 15 at 9:00PM EDT by NWS Northern Indiana</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>SVRIWX

The National Weather Service in Northern Indiana has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northwestern Allen County in northeastern Indiana...
Southeastern Noble County in northeastern Indiana...
Southwestern De Kalb County in northeastern Indiana...

* Until 900 PM EDT.

* At 816 PM EDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line
extending from 6 miles southwest of Avilla to Churubusco to near
Columbia City, moving east at 25 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Fort Wayne, Huntertown, Ege, Ari, Wallen, Lake Everett, and Laotto.

This includes Interstate 69 in Indiana between mile markers 310 and
312, and between mile markers 317 and 323.</Snippet>
