   <name>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 15 at 7:15PM CDT until September 15 at 7:45PM CDT by NWS Kansas City/Pleasant Hill MO</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>SVREAX

The National Weather Service in Pleasant Hill has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Northeastern Cass County in west central Missouri...

* Until 745 PM CDT.

* At 715 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Pleasant
Hill, moving north at 15 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Lee's Summit, Raymore, Harrisonville, Pleasant Hill, Greenwood,
Peculiar, Lake Winnebago, East Lynne, Baldwin Park, and Strasburg.

This includes Interstate 49 between mile markers 160 and 165.</Snippet>
