  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Advisory issued September 15 at 5:31PM MDT until September 15 at 8:30PM MDT by NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...Central Otero County in south central New Mexico...

* WHEN...Until 830 PM MDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
River or stream flows are elevated.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 529 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has
fallen. This same location already saw plentiful rain earlier
this afternoon which will make this area even more sensitive to
additional rainfall.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Mayhill and James Canyon.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
