  <Placemark>
   <name>Hazardous Seas Warning issued September 15 at 1:32PM PDT until September 15 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Medford OR</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_moderate</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Gusty north winds 15 to 25 kt with gusts up to 35 kt
and steep seas 6 to 8 ft. North winds increase some on
Tuesday, 20 to 30 kt with gusts to 35 kt and isolated areas of
gusts to 40 kt possible. Seas become steep to very steep, 7 to
10 ft at 8 seconds.

* WHERE...All areas. Very steep seas are expected within 5 to 30
nm from shore from Gold Beach southward.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 11 PM PDT
Wednesday. For the Hazardous Seas Warning, from 11 AM this
morning to 11 PM PDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Very steep and hazardous seas could capsize or
damage vessels. Bar crossings will become especially
treacherous.

* View the hazard area in detail at https://go.usa.gov/x6hks</Snippet>
